Development failures retained rather than hidden
- Initial new test assumed the wrong starting ration count; replaced that assumption
  with comparison against the real existing enlistment configuration.
- Waiting until late afternoon caused real hunger death, not a family-duty meeting.
  Preserved it as an interruption case; a properly supplied branch proves refusal.
- Inserting visit into the injustice page broke its original four-choice UI contract.
  Kept the old assertions; moved visiting after the military-injustice decision.
- Early retreat was terminal in runtime but not hometown replay; now both freeze at
  the actual first_patrol_withdrawn boundary while legacy courier waits still work.
- Trusting time/consumption claims allowed a free hour and a fabricated local shortage.
  Replaced that trust with complete authoritative clock/event/state reconstruction.
- Fractional-time subtraction needed a bounded float tolerance for one-hour visits.
- Malformed old narrative payloads reached hometown code too early; original Youth
  validation now runs first. All 2,201 malformed-save checks pass without script errors.
- Unbounded replay advanced a sparse future before rejecting; now it compares after
  each hourly boundary. The final sparse-future regressions pass.
- First export still carried old macOS bundle metadata; corrected to 0.12.0 and reran.

PASS: independent final review of cf61ca6 / fb201ba3
Repeated new suites (291 / 53 / 35+27); original terminal/free-hour/false-shortage
reproductions; coordinated exact-day fake rations; live-battle load/continue 14;
malformed source payloads 90. No script errors or remaining slice blocker found.
Sparse future variants each stopped at 418 total reconstructed events (406 input
history entries), rather than simulating 698/2,718 events before rejecting.
Those figures are total replay lengths, not counts of additional events.

